<title>UK: UK postal workers vote to resume strikes.</title>
<headline>UK postal workers vote to resume strikes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British postal workers belonging to the Communication Workers' union have voted in favour of resuming strike action in their long running dispute with Royal Mail, the Press Association reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The PA said 61 percent of postal workers had voted in favour of resuming the strikes, which led the government temporarily to suspend Royal Mail's monopoly earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
